WEBVTT

00:12.971 --> 00:14.014
I'm home.

00:14.931 --> 00:15.932
Yota!

00:16.599 --> 00:18.935
- I'm so sorry about earlier.
- Huh?

00:19.644 --> 00:22.439
You must feel annoyed for a family member
to come and talk to you

00:22.522 --> 00:24.065
when you're with a friend.

00:24.607 --> 00:25.608
MUMBLE MUMBLE

00:25.692 --> 00:28.069
Oh, goodness. And you are at that age...

00:28.153 --> 00:30.905
- No. It's fine.
- Why did I call out to you?

00:34.743 --> 00:36.494
Thanks for the food.

00:38.038 --> 00:39.122
Come on, now.

00:40.081 --> 00:42.417
No fair! Haruto's getting all the fun.

00:42.500 --> 00:44.419
Could you wait until I'm done eating?

00:44.502 --> 00:47.046
- Now!
- So loud!

00:48.757 --> 00:50.717
You two...

00:50.800 --> 00:51.801
RUMBLE RUMBLE

00:51.885 --> 00:52.886
WHOOSH

00:52.969 --> 00:55.305
- Stop bothering your brother!
- Daddy!

00:57.891 --> 01:00.643
- Do the airplane again!
- Do it!

01:00.727 --> 01:02.812
- Daddy's done for now.
- Come on!

01:02.896 --> 01:04.397
Wanna tag out?

01:04.481 --> 01:07.067
You don't have to do anything, Yota.

01:07.150 --> 01:08.151
You kids.

01:08.234 --> 01:09.235
Thanks.

01:14.866 --> 01:16.034
Daddy!

01:16.117 --> 01:17.827
NOISY NOISY

01:24.793 --> 01:29.714
The sounds of the day
swirl around and around in my head.

01:36.346 --> 01:38.181
I have to stop the noise,

01:39.390 --> 01:40.892
or it consumes me.

01:42.769 --> 01:43.853
Nothing.

01:45.647 --> 01:47.482
Think of nothing.

01:51.945 --> 01:55.031
I have one little sister,
and one little brother.

01:55.115 --> 01:57.450
And I tell you what, man,
are they stubborn!

01:57.992 --> 02:00.829
We were trying to decide
what to have for dinner the other day,

02:00.912 --> 02:04.624
and my sister said, "I want pasta!"
but my brother said, "I want curry!"

02:04.707 --> 02:07.127
Neither would budge. And then...

02:07.210 --> 02:09.838
My younger brother and sister
are still little.

02:09.921 --> 02:11.631
It's too noisy at home.

02:12.465 --> 02:14.884
- Have you been out here all this time?
- Yeah.

02:17.887 --> 02:20.765
But I want to spend some time zoning out.

02:21.933 --> 02:24.519
The more I think about it,

02:25.728 --> 02:28.690
the more the words he's said
start falling into place.

02:30.650 --> 02:32.652
But even if I am right about this,

02:33.945 --> 02:36.489
is this really something
I should be getting involved in?

02:37.949 --> 02:40.994
If someone says they're fine,

02:41.578 --> 02:43.163
who am I to worry?

02:44.747 --> 02:47.167
Who am I to intrude further?

04:19.550 --> 04:23.930
EPISODE 7
LONELINESS AND SOLITUDE

04:24.013 --> 04:25.306
YUISHIRO

04:25.390 --> 04:26.849
Listen, Koyuki.

04:27.475 --> 04:30.353
Your father and I are getting a divorce.

04:32.188 --> 04:33.189
LOVEBIRDS

04:33.273 --> 04:37.360
I knew they weren't like those
perfect couples you see on TV.

04:37.443 --> 04:38.736
I don't think that.

04:38.820 --> 04:43.116
- I knew they argued when I wasn't looking.
- I work myself to the bone, you know?

04:43.700 --> 04:47.328
I knew. I knew all this.

04:49.080 --> 04:50.832
And yet...

04:51.916 --> 04:54.085
I still felt safe in the knowledge

04:54.877 --> 04:58.131
that Mom and I were close,
and that Dad loved me.

04:59.090 --> 05:02.427
I felt confident that those things
would keep them together.

05:04.053 --> 05:06.597
I thought it would all work out.

05:07.598 --> 05:09.642
But was I in fact someone...

05:11.269 --> 05:12.270
YUISHIRO - HIKAWA

05:13.104 --> 05:15.231
...that Dad could live without?

05:20.320 --> 05:22.864
Her water bottle is so lame.
Like, it literally makes me laugh.

05:22.947 --> 05:24.741
Stop it, Manatsu.

05:26.367 --> 05:28.369
I didn't fit in.

05:28.453 --> 05:32.290
I never felt like I belonged,
no matter where I went.

05:33.458 --> 05:37.587
Koyun, what do you find
so repulsive about Igarashi?

05:37.670 --> 05:38.796
I feel sorry for the guy.

05:40.465 --> 05:43.801
I felt empty, not being able
to share my feelings with anyone.

05:44.969 --> 05:46.304
I thought what if...

05:47.096 --> 05:52.769
What if nobody really cares
whether I'm around or not?

05:54.020 --> 05:57.023
The thoughts crept in,

05:57.607 --> 05:59.442
and slowly tore at my heart.

06:01.402 --> 06:03.821
CLUB WITHDRAWAL FORM

06:09.452 --> 06:10.912
Back then,

06:12.205 --> 06:14.624
being with others
was when I felt most alone.

06:19.921 --> 06:22.340
GRADE 1 CLASS 2

06:22.423 --> 06:23.424
WHEW... WHEW...

06:23.508 --> 06:24.592
Yota is not me.

06:25.301 --> 06:27.595
His circumstances
are completely different to mine.

06:27.678 --> 06:29.597
YOTA - WHAT TIME DO YOU FINISH
CLUB ACTIVITIES TODAY?

06:30.306 --> 06:34.602
What's right to me
and what's right to him may be different.

06:35.937 --> 06:38.689
But still, I feel like I understand.

06:39.190 --> 06:40.191
Go!

06:41.400 --> 06:45.113
I know how lonely it feels
to be around others

06:45.196 --> 06:47.198
and still feel like you don't belong.

06:50.660 --> 06:51.869
Koyun?

06:52.662 --> 06:57.500
Probably around dismiss--

07:01.087 --> 07:02.713
Hey, your phone!

07:04.715 --> 07:05.758
Geez.

07:06.467 --> 07:07.552
KOYUKI

07:07.635 --> 07:08.970
Koyun?

07:09.053 --> 07:12.014
Sorry about that. Thank you.

07:13.224 --> 07:14.517
I saw it.

07:16.602 --> 07:18.521
PROBABLY AN UPRISING

07:19.105 --> 07:20.982
What does that mean?

07:22.859 --> 07:23.860
PROBABLY AROUND DISMISSAL

07:23.943 --> 07:25.278
SORRY, TYPO! LOL

07:26.654 --> 07:28.281
PFFT

07:28.364 --> 07:30.533
BLAZING CHINESE GYOSHO

07:31.492 --> 07:36.247
And then I dropped my phone
before I could fix it, and it sent.

07:37.498 --> 07:40.042
I was like, "What kind of typo was that?"

07:40.126 --> 07:41.127
BIG HANDS

07:41.210 --> 07:43.546
I'm not very good at typing on my phone.

07:44.130 --> 07:45.131
Grandpa.

07:45.214 --> 07:47.633
I have superseded "Dad" now.

07:50.636 --> 07:52.722
Sorry for dragging you out like this.

07:52.805 --> 07:54.056
I don't mind.

07:59.520 --> 08:00.771
So...

08:01.355 --> 08:02.565
My...

08:03.316 --> 08:04.817
My parents are divorced.

08:04.901 --> 08:05.902
Huh?

08:09.739 --> 08:12.116
Which means I'm on my own a lot
when I get home.

08:13.242 --> 08:16.204
So if you're free,
and it doesn't have to be all the time,

08:18.164 --> 08:21.792
but I'd really like it
if you'd help me kill time after school.

08:26.297 --> 08:27.465
I'd like that.

08:31.385 --> 08:33.471
That's very kind of you, Koyun.

08:33.554 --> 08:35.306
Huh? No, it's not.

08:35.389 --> 08:37.725
I'm so narrow-minded,
and I'm quick to anger.

08:37.808 --> 08:39.227
That's not true.

08:42.313 --> 08:45.233
I see you as a kind person.

08:49.237 --> 08:50.238
Sorry, but...

08:51.489 --> 08:54.492
can we have a chat for a little?

08:55.660 --> 08:56.661
Sure.

09:03.626 --> 09:08.130
Ever since Mom passed away,
Dad has always been super busy.

09:08.756 --> 09:11.509
He never makes it
to any school events either.

09:12.343 --> 09:14.762
PARENT VISITATION DAY

09:15.471 --> 09:19.183
I tried not to think about it
during parent visitation days.

09:19.267 --> 09:20.268
FIDGETY
LOOKY LOOKY

09:24.814 --> 09:25.898
And then...

09:25.982 --> 09:28.651
Hello, Yota. It's nice to meet you.

09:29.360 --> 09:30.903
You're very tall.

09:30.987 --> 09:32.280
This is Akari.

09:33.030 --> 09:36.534
Dad introduced me to my current mom.

09:37.910 --> 09:40.121
Sorry, he's very shy around others.

09:40.204 --> 09:42.123
Yota. No need to force it, okay?

09:42.206 --> 09:43.791
UM... UM...

09:44.917 --> 09:48.129
Mom is very nice to me.

09:55.386 --> 09:56.387
But...

09:58.139 --> 10:00.558
Akari! I think I can get
my paternity leave.

10:01.142 --> 10:02.810
- Really?
- Yeah.

10:02.893 --> 10:05.521
- I'm so happy! Thank you.
- Finally.

10:06.230 --> 10:08.316
Sometimes I wonder.

10:09.358 --> 10:11.527
I told you so.

10:11.611 --> 10:13.654
Do I even exist?

10:15.281 --> 10:21.621
I feel like I'm the only one
who is different in my family.

10:24.373 --> 10:26.083
I know I'm probably
just being overdramatic,

10:27.376 --> 10:29.795
but once I start,
I can't stop thinking about it...

10:31.714 --> 10:33.299
I'm always running away from it.

10:39.263 --> 10:43.559
Yota. You can't blame yourself
for your thoughts or the way you feel.

10:44.060 --> 10:46.312
I get it so much that it hurts.

10:47.438 --> 10:51.317
You may be wrestling with
"why do I think like this?"

10:52.777 --> 10:55.237
But the more you blame yourself,

10:55.905 --> 10:59.241
you start to despise yourself, right?

10:59.742 --> 11:03.621
You can run away from your environment,
but you can't run away from yourself.

11:06.207 --> 11:08.125
You're amazing, Koyun.

11:10.127 --> 11:11.337
You see right through me.

11:22.348 --> 11:24.767
Hey, Koyun? You're crying?

11:24.850 --> 11:27.269
Don't mind me.

11:27.353 --> 11:30.940
This is just like a glitch in my system
when I can't process my emotions.

11:31.023 --> 11:33.150
- What?
- I get it all the time.

11:33.234 --> 11:34.443
Huh?

11:35.778 --> 11:38.364
He is different in gender,
in build, and in personality.

11:38.948 --> 11:42.243
He is so different to me,
and I envied him for that.

11:43.869 --> 11:49.250
I thought Yota's kindness came
from his strength of heart and composure.

11:50.709 --> 11:53.671
But if it's because he bottles things in,
or if he's given up already...

11:54.880 --> 11:57.383
That would be heartbreaking for him.

11:59.844 --> 12:03.139
Yota. You don't have to be
a "good" person.

12:05.349 --> 12:08.018
So please don't torture yourself.

12:13.607 --> 12:16.527
SIGH

12:17.403 --> 12:21.198
Thank you, Koyun.
Sorry for talking about such weird things.

12:21.740 --> 12:23.909
No, it's not weird at all.

12:25.286 --> 12:28.122
I've never talked about this
with anyone before.

12:29.123 --> 12:32.001
Definitely never talked about it
with Minato, or anyone like that.

12:32.084 --> 12:36.172
You really love Amamiya, don't you?

12:37.381 --> 12:38.382
Not really?

12:38.966 --> 12:40.301
If you say so.

12:41.427 --> 12:44.680
And if I can be of any help,
I'm all ears if you need me.

12:45.890 --> 12:48.934
When you bottle things in, your heart...
It, like...

12:49.477 --> 12:52.146
It eventually just gets covered in soot.

12:52.646 --> 12:53.689
Soot?

12:53.772 --> 12:55.191
Yes. Soot.

12:55.274 --> 12:58.110
When it builds up,
it clouds your outlook on life.

12:58.194 --> 13:00.696
- Before you know it, you're stuck.
- Soot, soot!

13:01.197 --> 13:03.032
Soot, soot...

13:04.658 --> 13:05.910
I see.

13:05.993 --> 13:07.244
That does make sense.

13:19.548 --> 13:20.925
What do I do?

13:23.511 --> 13:25.971
Koyun. I gotta tell you.

13:35.606 --> 13:36.857
I...

13:38.817 --> 13:41.612
I'm in love.

13:43.781 --> 13:44.782
What?

13:53.916 --> 13:56.752
I'm in love.

13:58.879 --> 13:59.880
What?

14:02.550 --> 14:04.760
With Miki...

14:12.476 --> 14:14.395
What? What?

14:14.478 --> 14:18.315
You mean "love" love? Not like? "Love"?

14:18.399 --> 14:19.400
PANIC - EEK

14:24.238 --> 14:25.406
Both.

14:27.491 --> 14:28.909
No way.

14:28.993 --> 14:30.995
I had no idea!

14:31.078 --> 14:33.080
But you're always so calm?

14:33.581 --> 14:36.041
No, I'm really not.

14:36.542 --> 14:37.543
PANICKING INSIDE

14:37.626 --> 14:40.421
I'm always a total mess
whenever I'm around Miki.

14:41.005 --> 14:43.424
What? No, you're no--

14:49.096 --> 14:50.097
You are.

14:50.598 --> 14:52.224
MIDDLE SCHOOL
DO YOU LIKE MIKI?

14:52.308 --> 14:54.184
Minato's known for a while now.

14:54.268 --> 14:55.853
- NO, WHY WOULD YOU SAY THAT?
- YEAH, RIGHT...

14:55.936 --> 14:57.479
But he bugs me, so I just deny it.

14:57.563 --> 14:59.523
I guess you would feel embarrassed.

15:00.441 --> 15:04.445
Wow, now what? This makes me so happy!

15:05.905 --> 15:08.240
What's the real me?

15:08.741 --> 15:10.868
I don't know what I'm feeling anymore.

15:10.951 --> 15:15.289
Don't go creating an ideal version of me
and then get disappointed!

15:15.372 --> 15:16.373
GRRR!

15:16.457 --> 15:20.836
Miki. Somebody likes you for you.
Just the way you are.

15:21.962 --> 15:25.132
And he's such a wonderful person.

15:28.218 --> 15:29.219
FIDGET FIDGET

15:29.303 --> 15:31.555
Are you going to ask her out?

15:31.639 --> 15:34.475
Koyun? Where did all
this energy come from?

15:34.558 --> 15:36.060
Sorry. I'm just happy.

15:36.143 --> 15:37.144
(SUPER HAPPY DANCE)

15:37.895 --> 15:38.896
But...

15:43.275 --> 15:44.860
How does Miki feel?

15:46.987 --> 15:48.864
I haven't thought that far ahead.

15:50.449 --> 15:53.243
Or rather,
I don't even plan on telling her.

15:54.536 --> 15:57.748
I just like her. I like Miki.

15:59.041 --> 16:01.794
And I value her as a friend as well.

16:03.212 --> 16:07.841
I know she probably
doesn't see me in the same way.

16:09.301 --> 16:10.386
But...

16:11.220 --> 16:15.057
I feel like as time goes on,
it feels like I'm just deceiving her.

16:16.225 --> 16:19.645
I'm starting to feel like I need
to apologize for liking her.

16:19.728 --> 16:20.854
WHOA!

16:20.938 --> 16:23.232
Didn't I tell you not to torture yourself?

16:23.315 --> 16:24.525
Soot, soot...

16:27.611 --> 16:29.863
Don't tell anybody
what we talked about today.

16:29.947 --> 16:31.031
Of course I won't.

16:31.615 --> 16:35.494
I'm absolutely rooting for you,
but I won't do anything to give you away.

16:36.912 --> 16:37.913
Thanks.

16:41.500 --> 16:42.835
Feels like a thumb.

16:42.918 --> 16:43.961
It is my pinky.

16:45.504 --> 16:49.466
I'm glad we became friends, Koyun.

16:53.512 --> 16:54.513
Me too.

16:57.474 --> 16:59.309
Yota, welcome home.

16:59.393 --> 17:00.561
I'm home.

17:01.395 --> 17:03.063
STARE

17:03.605 --> 17:05.190
Did you take a detour home?

17:05.274 --> 17:06.275
EEP

17:06.358 --> 17:08.193
Did I get home too late?

17:08.277 --> 17:10.946
Yeah, I was with a friend.

17:11.030 --> 17:12.197
I knew it.

17:12.281 --> 17:16.952
You look happy, so I thought
something good must have happened.

17:17.036 --> 17:18.037
Huh?

17:18.620 --> 17:20.873
- Yota!
- Kids!

17:20.956 --> 17:21.957
PIT PAT

17:22.833 --> 17:24.710
You gotta dry your hair first.

17:24.793 --> 17:26.086
Good grief.

17:26.170 --> 17:30.716
- Yota always just goes off to his room.
- Yeah!

17:30.799 --> 17:32.718
So we came to see you.

17:32.801 --> 17:35.929
- Yota, Yota...
- Go dry your hair. I'll wait.

17:36.013 --> 17:37.723
- You will?
- Yes.

17:37.806 --> 17:39.850
WHOOSH

17:39.933 --> 17:41.226
Goodness...

17:41.852 --> 17:45.647
Yota. There's ice cream in the freezer.
It's the good kind.

17:46.273 --> 17:48.484
But dinner first, okay?

17:48.567 --> 17:50.235
HMPH!

17:52.613 --> 17:56.909
The kindness of others
is slowly seeping into my heart.

17:59.703 --> 18:03.207
How did I ever think I didn't belong?

18:04.583 --> 18:05.751
Soot...

18:07.628 --> 18:11.882
I see it now. I never realized it before.

18:14.426 --> 18:16.512
It's quiet tonight.

18:18.388 --> 18:19.848
It's been a while.

18:22.601 --> 18:23.936
BREAD

18:24.019 --> 18:25.521
Did you sleep well last night?

18:25.604 --> 18:27.439
Yep. Like a log.

18:27.523 --> 18:28.524
I see.

18:30.192 --> 18:31.276
Huh?

18:32.027 --> 18:33.612
You got the drinks?

18:34.279 --> 18:35.280
Yeah.

18:35.364 --> 18:38.283
Hi, Amamiya. It's been a while.

18:39.701 --> 18:41.286
It has.

18:42.371 --> 18:43.372
What's this?

18:43.872 --> 18:45.833
It's my trio!

18:46.458 --> 18:48.293
- What a haul.
- What a haul.

18:49.461 --> 18:51.880
You're having bread
from the school store for lunch too?

18:51.964 --> 18:55.968
Get a load of this.
I left my lunch by the door at home today.

18:56.051 --> 18:57.177
Oh, dear.

18:57.261 --> 18:59.054
What? They still had sweet red bean buns?

18:59.138 --> 19:00.806
Yeah. Do you want it?

19:00.889 --> 19:02.891
No, no. I'll pay you. How much?

19:02.975 --> 19:03.976
WATCHING

19:04.059 --> 19:06.812
MIFFED

19:09.189 --> 19:10.816
HMM...

19:11.525 --> 19:13.193
It's fine. You can have it.

19:13.277 --> 19:15.154
No, let me pay.

19:15.237 --> 19:16.280
Then let's say, ten yen?

19:16.363 --> 19:18.448
No way was it ten yen.
Then let's at least trade.

19:19.408 --> 19:20.409
TUG

19:21.243 --> 19:22.578
Amamiya.

19:23.704 --> 19:25.581
What did you do over the winter break?

19:26.540 --> 19:28.000
She initiated conversation.

19:29.293 --> 19:32.796
I guess I mostly did club activities.

19:33.589 --> 19:36.341
I hung out with some classmates a bit,

19:36.842 --> 19:38.594
and took my dog for walks.

19:38.677 --> 19:39.887
Dog.

19:39.970 --> 19:41.096
FUZZY - DOG

19:42.222 --> 19:43.348
What else?

19:44.224 --> 19:49.313
I always seem to put my foot in my mouth
whenever I talk to her.

19:50.314 --> 19:52.733
I never know what to do.

19:53.775 --> 19:57.738
Hey. You got a name?

19:57.821 --> 19:58.822
Huh? Me?

19:58.906 --> 20:00.657
No. For the dog.

20:03.118 --> 20:05.078
Your first name is Minato, right?

20:08.373 --> 20:10.751
- It's Ponta.
- Huh?

20:10.834 --> 20:14.171
The dog! My name's not Ponta.

20:14.254 --> 20:15.797
What am I even saying?

20:15.881 --> 20:17.507
FLUSTER FLUSTER
PONTA AMAMIYA - PONTA

20:21.386 --> 20:23.972
Amamiya's first name... is "Ponta."

20:24.056 --> 20:27.142
Hey, could you not lose it over that?

20:28.393 --> 20:29.478
Sorry.

20:29.561 --> 20:30.646
SWEET RED BEAN BUN

20:30.729 --> 20:33.607
You really like your sweet red beans.
Don't you, Miki?

20:34.107 --> 20:36.485
Can't go wrong with sweet red beans!

20:36.568 --> 20:37.736
Right, Koyu--

20:37.819 --> 20:40.239
- Is Ponta doing well?
- Yeah.

20:40.322 --> 20:42.074
- I'm always taking photos.
- Am I...

20:42.157 --> 20:43.867
- Yeah?
- Am I being a third wheel?

20:43.951 --> 20:45.118
SHOCK

20:45.202 --> 20:46.703
Koyun!

20:48.080 --> 20:49.081
WHOMP - TAKE THAT - AH

20:49.164 --> 20:50.749
What was that for?

20:50.832 --> 20:51.833
SIGH

20:51.917 --> 20:54.169
I just got a surge of energy.

20:54.253 --> 20:56.672
That's your reason? You're dangerous.

20:58.757 --> 21:00.425
- Hey.
- I'm sorry.

21:00.509 --> 21:02.761
- You don't gotta force it.
- It's fine.

21:03.262 --> 21:04.346
SMILE GUARD

21:04.429 --> 21:05.931
Sorry. I couldn't help it.

21:06.515 --> 21:08.892
Now, look here! Don't make that face.

21:08.976 --> 21:09.977
SMILE GUARD ALPHA

21:10.060 --> 21:11.186
I'm sorry. I'm sorry!

21:11.270 --> 21:12.854
What's this?

21:13.647 --> 21:15.023
Koyun and Yota...

21:16.608 --> 21:19.444
- They're getting on so well.
- They're getting on so well.

21:19.528 --> 21:21.154
TODAY'S RECOMMENDATION
SAVORY BREAD FAIR

21:21.238 --> 21:22.447
I'll be going now.

21:22.531 --> 21:23.991
You're eating in again?

21:25.200 --> 21:27.369
- Yeah.
- Eat in where?

21:27.452 --> 21:28.620
NORIKO FROM THE NURSE'S OFFICE

21:28.704 --> 21:30.831
The nurse's office is not a café!

21:31.873 --> 21:33.208
I'll see you later.

21:33.834 --> 21:34.835
See you later.

21:39.298 --> 21:44.177
Two people I like very much
seem to be hitting it off.

21:44.261 --> 21:45.804
That's all this is, so...

21:47.014 --> 21:50.726
So why does it get me so excited?

21:52.060 --> 21:54.855
So, hey.
I know this is still a long ways off.

21:54.938 --> 21:58.317
But shall we have another four-way
study session for the end-of-year exams?

22:02.821 --> 22:04.990
- Sure.
- Hooray!

22:05.574 --> 22:07.909
I'm gonna set those two up!

22:07.993 --> 22:08.994
SO EXCITED

22:11.079 --> 22:13.832
- Hey, isn't that Miki?
- Okay! Time to study hard.

22:13.915 --> 22:18.253
And isn't that Hino and Amamiya with her?

22:19.838 --> 22:24.092
Is that how Miki usually behaves?

23:50.345 --> 23:55.350
Subtitle translation by: Rychelle Brittain
